pageType: content
background: { type: solid, color: "$paper" }
notes: |
  Slide 10: Open Science Workflow: From Strain HDF5 to Gravitational Wave Data Center.
  - Details the open-science architecture enabling global research:
    1. Low-latency alert streaming (<30s) via GCN Kafka notices, distributing sky localization maps and classification parameters worldwide.
    2. Bulk open-access archival data distributed by the Gravitational Wave Open Science Center (GWOSC.org), providing 4 kHz and 16 kHz calibrated strain h(t) files in HDF5 and Frame formats.
    3. Community open-source Python stack (PyCBC, GWpy, Bilby, LALSuite) guaranteeing 100% end-to-end computational reproducibility.
  - Explains the data volume (~1 PB across observing runs) and the open data commons licensing policy.
